powerpagecomponent.content:
{
  "source": "{% comment %}
  The AQS check's notes, read-only, for the adviser (project owner, 2026-09-30: "Case Notes
  and Even better if need to show on the remedial page for the adviser"). Include with:

    (% include 'OT AQS Notes' case_id: cid %)

  TWO questions, both in the AQS grading section, both plain text:

    Q-GR-03  "Case Notes"
    Q-GR-04  "Even Better If..."

  Modelled on 'OT Tax Notes', and it keeps that template's rules for the same reasons:

  - Only SUBMITTED AQS reviews are read. A draft is work in progress, and a half-written note
    in front of an adviser as though it were the finding is worse than nothing.
  - Nothing is drawn when both boxes are empty, or the case has no submitted AQS check yet: an
    empty panel headed "AQS check notes" reads as a fault.
  - Every submitted AQS review is rendered, not one. A recheck leaves a case with more than
    one, and this Liquid applies no cross-entity order, so "the latest" would be an arbitrary
    one. When there is more than one, each note carries its check's submission date.
  - Plain text is escaped with its line breaks kept. Both questions are multi-line text, so
    their answers are in al_answertext and that is the only answer column the fetch asks for:
    the server refuses a formatted answer on a question that is not Rich text
    (ResponseRules), so al_answerrichtext can never be filled for them, and
    Check-PortalTemplates.ps1 fails a fetch that selects a column none of its questions can
    fill. The rich-text branch below is kept so the panel still reads as the Tax panel does,
    and it is never taken while the column is not fetched. If either question is ever
    retyped to Rich text, add al_answerrichtext back to the fetch; the same check fails
    until it is.

  Unlike the Tax panel, every note is labelled, not only when there are several: the two
  questions ask different things, and an adviser should not have to guess which one a
  paragraph answers.

  Styled with the Tax panel's classes (ot-tax-notes__*) so the two panels read as a pair and
  the site's stylesheet did not need to change.

  Nothing here is editable. The AQS review is submitted and locked by the time either page
  that includes this is read.
{% endcomment %}

{% if case_id and case_id != '' %}
  {% fetchxml ot_aqs_notes %}
  <fetch>
    <entity name="al_response">
      <attribute name="al_responseid" />
      <attribute name="al_answertext" />
      <link-entity name="al_questionversion" from="al_questionversionid" to="al_questionversionid" alias="qv">
        <link-entity name="al_question" from="al_questionid" to="al_questionid" alias="q">
          <attribute name="al_questioncode" />
          <filter type="and">
            <condition attribute="al_questioncode" operator="in">
              <value>Q-GR-03</value>
              <value>Q-GR-04</value>
            </condition>
          </filter>
        </link-entity>
      </link-entity>
      <link-entity name="al_reviewinstance" from="al_reviewinstanceid" to="al_reviewinstanceid" alias="ri">
        <attribute name="al_reviewinstanceid" />
        <attribute name="al_submittedon" />
        <filter type="and">
          <condition attribute="al_outcomecaseid" operator="eq" value="{{ case_id | xml_escape }}" />
          <condition attribute="al_reviewtype" operator="eq" value="120910201" />
          <condition attribute="al_submittedon" operator="not-null" />
        </filter>
      </link-entity>
    </entity>
  </fetch>
  {% endfetchxml %}

  {% comment %}
    Counted before anything is drawn, so a check whose boxes were left empty opens no panel.
    A response row can exist carrying a blank answer - the form writes one as soon as a
    question is touched - so the test is on the text, not on the row. The same pass notes
    whether the notes come from more than one check, which decides whether they are dated.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% assign ot_aqs_note_count = 0 %}
  {% assign ot_aqs_first_review = '' %}
  {% assign ot_aqs_multi = false %}
  {% for r in ot_aqs_notes.results.entities %}
    {% assign ot_note_text = r.al_answertext | default: '' | strip %}
    {% assign ot_note_rich = r.al_answerrichtext | default: '' | strip %}
    {% if ot_note_text != '' or ot_note_rich != '' %}
      {% assign ot_aqs_note_count = ot_aqs_note_count | plus: 1 %}
      {% assign ot_note_review = r['ri.al_reviewinstanceid'] | append: '' %}
      {% if ot_aqs_first_review == '' %}
        {% assign ot_aqs_first_review = ot_note_review %}
      {% elsif ot_note_review != ot_aqs_first_review %}
        {% assign ot_aqs_multi = true %}
      {% endif %}
    {% endif %}
  {% endfor %}

  {% if ot_aqs_note_count > 0 %}
  <section class="ot-card ot-tax-notes ot-aqs-notes" aria-labelledby="ot-aqs-notes-heading">
    <h2 class="ot-card__title" id="ot-aqs-notes-heading">AQS check notes</h2>
    <p class="ot-tax-notes__intro">
      Recorded by the AQS checker when the AQS check was submitted. Read-only here.
    </p>
    {% comment %}Case Notes first, then Even Better If, whatever order the rows came back in.{% endcomment %}
    {% assign ot_aqs_codes = 'Q-GR-03,Q-GR-04' | split: ',' %}
    {% for ot_code in ot_aqs_codes %}
      {% for r in ot_aqs_notes.results.entities %}
        {% assign ot_note_text = r.al_answertext | default: '' | strip %}
        {% assign ot_note_rich = r.al_answerrichtext | default: '' | strip %}
        {% if r['q.al_questioncode'] == ot_code %}{% if ot_note_text != '' or ot_note_rich != '' %}
      <div class="ot-tax-notes__item">
        <p class="ot-tax-notes__meta">
          {% if ot_code == 'Q-GR-04' %}Even Better If...{% else %}Case Notes{% endif %}{% if ot_aqs_multi %} &mdash;
          AQS check submitted {{ r['ri.al_submittedon'] | date: 'dd MMM yyyy' | default: 'date not recorded' }}{% endif %}
        </p>
        {% if ot_note_rich != '' %}
        <div class="ot-tax-notes__text ot-rte__read">{{ ot_note_rich }}</div>
        {% else %}
        <p class="ot-tax-notes__text">{{ ot_note_text | escape | newline_to_br }}</p>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
        {% endif %}{% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
    {% endfor %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}
"
}
